{#
    A dialog of the panel: a title, a body and the buttons under it, with one form around them when
    it posts. Meant for {% embed %}: the page fills the body and footer blocks.

    The same template serves twice. A link with data-admin-modal opens its address in the modal of
    the layout (src/admin/js/modal.js), and the controller answers that request with the dialog
    alone; a plain visit gets it as a page of its own (components/ui/dialog-page.twig). That is why
    "close" is a link: in the modal data-bs-dismiss closes it, on the page it leads back.

    @param string title
    @param string close_url Where closing leads when the dialog is a page.
    @param string action    The address the form posts to, with the token; empty for no form.

    Blocks: body, footer.
#}
{% set action = action|default('') %}
{% if action %}
    <form class="modal-content" method="post" action="{{ action }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ app.csrf_token }}">
{% else %}
    <div class="modal-content">
{% endif %}
        <div class="modal-header">
            <h2 class="modal-title">{{ title }}</h2>
            <a href="{{ close_url }}" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="{{ d__('admin', 'Close') }}"></a>
        </div>
        <div class="modal-body">
            {% block body %}{% endblock %}
        </div>
        <div class="modal-footer">
            {% block footer %}{% endblock %}
        </div>
{% if action %}
    </form>
{% else %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
